{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_one_transaction_per_engineering_change", "label": "One Transaction per Engineering Change", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_adr_0145", "label": "ADR-0145", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One store authoritative; every engineering change happens exactly one way: project, commit, apply under one domain-wide write lock. Compensation code could only shrink the memory/disk gap, never close it."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_engineeringdomaincontext_executewriteasync", "label": "EngineeringDomainContext.ExecuteWriteAsync", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_project_commit_apply", "label": "Project Commit Apply", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Project the next state (may refuse, nothing touched), commit it with everything that goes with it and the audit row in one transaction, then apply to memory only after commit and while still holding the lock so the next writer projects from it."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_domain_wide_write_lock", "label": "Domain-Wide Write Lock", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One SemaphoreSlim for every engineering write: TempestOS is single-user, one process, saves seconds apart, and graph checks read unbounded slices that fine-grained locking would need an order-sensitive discipline over. First thing to revisit if multi-user."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_td_147_release_blocking", "label": "TD-147 Release Blocking", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An object creation whose initial durable write failed still registered the object in memory, so its next successful write made a reported failure real; the only Release Blocking row in BACKLOG history."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_engineeringobjectfactory_t__createasync", "label": "EngineeringObjectFactory<T>.CreateAsync", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_engineeringobjectbase", "label": "EngineeringObjectBase", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_engineeringobjectbase_state_cs", "label": "EngineeringObjectBase.State.cs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mutators decide when a change becomes durable, the state file decides what it is: different reasons to change, so different files."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_compensation_code_deleted", "label": "Compensation Code Deleted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Roughly 1,802 lines of RollBackOnFailureAsync, MutationRollbackPoint, write-intent store and reconciliation sweep deleted: restoring an in-memory field cannot unwrite a record already committed to disk."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_inmemoryengineeringobjectrepository_as_cache", "label": "InMemoryEngineeringObjectRepository as Cache", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_inmemoryengineeringdocumentstore_deleted", "label": "InMemoryEngineeringDocumentStore Deleted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeping a test-only second document store meant a fourth writer reintroduced purely to test a design whose point is that there are no longer four."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_five_writers_no_boundary", "label": "Five Writers No Boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "More than one writer and no boundary around them: the shared defect behind TD-135, TD-136 and TD-140 through TD-150."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_lost_update_reopened", "label": "Lost Update Reopened", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applying memory after the lock was released let a second writer read a committed-but-unapplied field; fixed by moving afterCommit inside the lock hold."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_gatedpersistencestore", "label": "GatedPersistenceStore", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parks one writer at the very end of its transaction with everything staged and both locks held, so a second writer wait is provable rather than merely likely."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_adversarial_test_rig", "label": "Adversarial Test Rig", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written to falsify ADR-0145, not demonstrate it: MutatorRefusalAdversarialTests, AttachmentRevisionAtomicityTests, RevisionAttachmentInterleavingTests."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_guard_rail_versus_characterisation", "label": "Guard-Rail versus Characterisation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A guard-rail must stay true for ever; a characterisation names a known defect and is inverted rather than deleted when fixed, so the suite still records what once was."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_icommandregistry_whenidleasync", "label": "ICommandRegistry.WhenIdleAsync", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Store disposal could pull the store from under a running command tail; WorkspaceManager.DisposeAsync waits up to ten seconds for in-flight invocations, counted from prompt open not dispatch."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_workspacemanager_disposeasync", "label": "WorkspaceManager.DisposeAsync", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_persistence_sequence_counter", "label": "Persistence Sequence Counter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_eager_rehydration_kept", "label": "Eager Rehydration Kept", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A lazy cache with two population paths is a second consistency problem, and this Work Package exists to remove one."}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_td_141", "label": "TD-141", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_td_150", "label": "TD-150", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_td_158", "label": "TD-158", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_td_23_td_32_verification_transaction", "label": "TD-23 TD-32 Verification Transaction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_wp_17_1b", "label": "WP 17.1B", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_wp_17_1a", "label": "WP 17.1A", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_one_transaction_per_engineering_change", "target": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_adr_0145", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_one_transaction_per_engineering_change", "target": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_engineeringdomaincontext_executewriteasync", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/academy/02 Runtime Architecture/54-one-transaction-per-engineering-change.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_academy_02_runtime_architecture_54_one_transaction_per_engineering_change_one_transactio